2.Add a custom font (such as 'Poppins' or 'Montserrat') to your Flutter app and update your ThemeData to use this font for all text in the app.
Add the font files to your assets, update pubspec.yaml, and set the fontFamily in ThemeData.

Step 1: Download the Poppins font files from 
Google Fonts — Poppins

Step 2: Create this folder structure in your project:
MyMusicTheme/
├── assets/
│   └── fonts/
│       ├── Poppins-Regular.ttf
│       └── Poppins-Bold.ttf
├── lib/
│   └── main.dart
└── pubspec.yaml

Step 3: Add the fonts to pubspec.yaml under flutter:.
flutter:
  uses-material-design: true
  fonts:
    - family: Poppins
      fonts:
        - asset: assets/fonts/Poppins-Regular.ttf
        - asset: assets/fonts/Poppins-Bold.ttf
          weight: 700

Step 4: Update your ThemeData in main.dart:
theme: ThemeData(
  fontFamily: 'Poppins',
  primaryColor: Colors.purple,
  colorScheme: ColorScheme.fromSeed(
    seedColor: Colors.purple,
    secondary: Colors.orange,
  ),
),
